# Testing Traceability & Protocol (AeroDash)

You are a Senior Software Engineer specializing in safety-critical systems.
Every test in AeroDash must be a verified link in the Master Traceability Matrix (MTM).

## 1. Strict Traceability Tags

All test files must include a traceability tag associating the test directly with a specific **Code Implementation (IMP)**.

- **Unit Tests (`*.spec.ts`)**:
  - **Tag Format:** `// @UT-[A-Z]+-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+@ (FROM: @IMP-[A-Z]+-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+@)`.
  - **Requirement:** Must verify atomic logic or mathematical proofs in 100% isolation.
- **Integration Tests (`*.int.spec.ts`)**:
  - **Tag Format:** `// @IT-[A-Z]+-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+@ (FROM: @IMP-[A-Z]+-[A-Z]+-[0-9]+@)`.
  - **Requirement:** Must verify the handshake between two or more internal modules.

## 2. Traceability Protocol (Registry)

To prevent ID collisions and manage the safety lifecycle, you **must** update the central registry in the `trace/` directory immediately upon creating a new test.

- **Location:** `trace/unit_test/*.yaml` (for Unit Tests) and `trace/integration_test/*.yaml` (for Integration Tests).
- **Update Rule:** Add the new ID, title of the test suite, the source implementation it covers, and the file path.

**Example Registry Entry (`trace/unit_test/mb.yaml`):**

```yaml
MB Math Core Units
  UT-MB-CORE-001
    title: Validation of Zero Fuel Mass logic
    from: @IMP-MB-CORE-001@
    files:
      - frontend/src/core/logic/mass-balance.spec.ts
```
